# tmux cheatsheet — personal config reminders
# Generated from tmux.conf.symlink (prefix: C-a)

---

## Prefix
  Prefix = **C-a** (remapped from default C-b)
  `prefix + a` or `prefix + C-a`  Send C-a to inner app (for nested tmux)

---

## Sessions
  `tmux new -s <name>`        New named session
  `tmux ls`                   List sessions
  `tmux attach -t <name>`     Attach to session
  `prefix + $`                Rename current session
  `prefix + d`                Detach from session
  `prefix + C-j`              Choose session tree (visual)
  `prefix + K`                Kill session, switch to next (never drops to bare terminal)
  `prefix + C-b`              Break pane into new named session (via tat), then exit

---

## Windows
  `prefix + c`                New window (in **current dir**)
  `prefix + ,`                Rename window
  `prefix + n` / `p`          Next / previous window
  `prefix + <number>`         Jump to window by index (starts at **1**, not 0)
  `prefix + b`                Break pane into new **detached** window

---

## Panes
### Navigation (no prefix!)
  **C-h**  **C-j**  **C-k**  **C-l**    Move left/down/up/right (vim-style)

### Resizing (no prefix!)
  **S-Left**  **S-Right**  **S-Down**  **S-Up**    Resize pane

### Splitting
  `prefix + -`                Split **vertical** (in current dir)
  `prefix + \`                Split **horizontal** (in current dir)

### Quick Panes (persistent)
  `prefix + h`                Open htop in horizontal split
  `prefix + D`                Open `docker stats` in horizontal split
  `prefix + L`                Open `tail -f log/development.log` in vertical split (current dir)

### Other
  `prefix + z`                Toggle pane zoom
  `prefix + x`                Kill pane

---

## Popups (floating, dismiss when done)
  `prefix + p`                Scratch shell popup (80% width, 70% height, current dir)
  `prefix + m`                Man page popup: prompts for page, displays at 80%x80%
  `prefix + =`                Calculator popup (`bc -l`) at 40%x30%

---
## Copy Mode (vi-style)
  `prefix + [`                Enter copy mode
  `v`                         Begin selection
  `y`                         Yank selection to **macOS clipboard** (pbcopy)
  `Enter`                     Copy selection to clipboard and exit
  `MouseDragEnd1Pane`         Copy selection to clipboard (mouse)
  `prefix + ]`                Paste from clipboard

---
## Config & Settings
  `prefix + r`                **Reload** tmux.conf
  **Base index:** Windows and panes start at **1** (not 0)
  **Mouse:** Enabled
  **History:** 50,000 lines scrollback
  **Display time:** 4 seconds (messages stay visible longer)
  **Pane borders:** Color #235 (inactive), #240 (active)
  **Stay in tmux:** Always — uses `tat` for new named sessions
